      "id": "rpohib1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. INTRODUCTION TO NARRATION"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Direct speech uses exact words enclosed in quotation marks, while indirect speech conveys the substance without quotes.",
        "Pronouns in indirect speech change using the SON rule: First person aligns with the Subject, Second person with the Object, and Third person undergoes No change.",
        "Tense backshift occurs when the reporting verb is in the past tense (e.g., Simple Present changes to Simple Past).",
        "Words indicating proximity in time and place shift to words expressing distance (e.g., 'now' to 'then', 'here' to 'there', 'today' to 'that day').",
        "Interrogative sentences convert from question form into assertive word order (Subject + Verb) without quotation or question marks."
      ],
      "id": "yq02kw6"
    },
