      "content": "17. HIGH-PROBABILITY SSC RULES"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Universal truths, habitual actions, and historical facts do NOT change tense even if the reporting verb is in the past tense.",
        "'Told' must always be followed by an object (e.g., 'He told me'), whereas 'said' does not take a direct personal object without 'to'.",
        "In indirect questions, conjunctions 'if' or 'whether' are used for Yes/No questions, while Wh- words act as conjunctions for Wh- questions."
